From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: msm8994: wait up to 10 s for the QCA6174 link

dw_pcie_wait_for_link() gives up after about 1 s, but the QCA6174 on this
platform trains a bit later than that (a manual rescan seconds afterwards
finds it). Keep polling before declaring the endpoint missing.

---
 drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -1052,6 +1052,16 @@ static void qcom_pcie_host_post_msm8994(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 
 		QTRACE(pci->dev, "P9 wait_for_link");
 		ret = dw_pcie_wait_for_link(pci);
+		if (ret) {
+			/* the QCA6174 trains slowly: keep polling for up to 10 s */
+			int tries;
+
+			for (tries = 0; tries < 100 && !dw_pcie_link_up(pci); tries++)
+				msleep(100);
+			if (dw_pcie_link_up(pci))
+				ret = 0;
+			QTRACE(pci->dev, "P9b link %s after %d ms extra", ret ? "down" : "up", tries * 100);
+		}
 		QTRACE(pci->dev, "P10 wait_for_link done ret=%d", ret);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(pci->dev, "endpoint did not answer (%d)\n", ret);
